<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Péronne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Péronne is a town on the Somme in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its castle was where Count Herbert II of Vermandois held King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> prisoner until his death in 929, and where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a> was forced to agree the Treaty of Péronne with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> in 1468. Heavily fought over in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, it houses the Historial de la Grande Guerre museum.</p></div>
